<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Finnish War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1808">1808</a>–<a href="/years/1809">1809</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleonic-wars">Napoleonic Wars</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Finnish War was fought from 1808 to 1809 between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a>, which invaded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/finland">Finland</a> after Sweden refused to join <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/continental-system">Continental System</a>. Russian forces took the fortress of Sveaborg and overran Finland. By the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-fredrikshamn">Treaty of Fredrikshamn</a> of 1809 Sweden ceded Finland, which became an autonomous grand duchy under the Russian tsar.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/finnish-war.jpg" alt="Finnish War" width="320" height="336" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Imonoz · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Finnish_War_Collage_5.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
